a doubt the most slides in the  end game credits for a fallout game at  29. some of these you may not even  achieve so you might not get all 29 but  there's 29 possible options to be shown  to you going back to novak for that  place you spend 20 minutes it has six  possible endings which all depend on the  faction you side with at the end of the  game and if you did the one quest  involved with no back called come fly  with me this one town has six endings  and even better one of my favorite  slides to convey this point is the  misfits when entering camp golf you may  find a group of ncr soldiers these guys  are the misfits terrible soldiers who  were stationed here since no one's going  to accept them they're lazy and  undisciplined and while you can talk to  them you have to speak to the sergeant  of the camp to actually start the quest  then you speak to all four of them  listen to what they think would improve  the squad's behavior then go with  whatever option you choose five minutes  to complete and has an end slide with  five different options if i asked you  would this group of four morons be  mentioned again after this quest is  completed you would probably say no and  that's what i thought when i first did  this mission but was surprised to see  them get their own slide at the end of  the game even the littlest of choices  count in new vegas and while some of  them have greater impact on the game  than others they purposely make those  small decisions matter by giving them  that end credit screen time so you're  constantly thinking about your own  choices for everything in the game in  most games that random person we do a  quest for for maybe two minutes will  never be mentioned again but obsidian  does not want you to think like this  they want you to really care about every  decision you make as it may have  consequences this will ultimately hook  the player and immerse them into the  world and makes everything feel more  fleshed out and real because of it  speaking of our decision or rather the  courier's decision in this case let's  discuss the dlc simply put i love this  game's dlc it does something not many  games do make its own story for example  skyrim story dlcs are dragonborn and  dawnguard each of them can be beaten at  any time and have no relation to the  overall story or the other dlc story  minus the fact that mirak does have ties  to you but still human being for a bit  fall new vegas doesn't do it this way  besides the fact that they made four dlc  with unique and separate stories not  related to each other they also dropped  hints and clues that would eventually  culminate into its own storyline some  claim there's a specific order to  playing these but i always felt that as  long as the lonesome road is last then  any order is fine but i've always played  them in the order of honest hearts old  world blues dead money then lonesome  road and that's how we'll be discussing  them now the first three all have a  separate story for the player to  experience but within them are clues and  hints that will eventually lead to the  last dlc they'll have the player stumble  into danger and get wound up into  something they'd never asked to be a  part of for honest hearts you can join  up with a caravan that gets ambushed and  now you're stuck in zion canyon with no  idea how to get back for old world blues  you're teleported to a place called big  mountain where the scientists there rip  out your brain in a dead money you're  captured by father elijah who will kill  you unless you work with him to open the  sierra madre casino all of these connect  to the lonesome road and the story of  the courier not much is known about the  courier we don't have much to go off of  other than the fact that that was our  job being a courier but obsidian decided  to build the storyline around this  question who really is the courier but  once again it wasn't until lonesome road  that any of this started making sense  honest hearts explores the ongoing  conflict between two tribes in a  completely foreign area it's different  from the mojave and thus is new to the  player we meet the tribe leaders joshua  graham and daniel both of whom are from  new canaan or as they call themselves  the new canaanites the new canaanites  were ambushed by the white legs and  driven into the zion canyon where they  meet the other tribes that we see them  leading in game this dlc is about us  resolving the conflict between the white  legs and the other two tribes old world  blues can be summed up in one word  bizarre it's the story of six scientists  who were constantly experimenting and  testing on literally anything they were  some of the smartest minds in the world  they eventually turned themselves into  robots so they could live indefinitely  and continue researching but their  research has started getting more  sinister for the entirety of the dlc we  work with the think tank to defeat  mobius until we realize that mobius  isn't the bad guy dr mobius informs us  other processing units when all the  doctors mobius included were made into  robots due to some recursion loop in  their programming they forgot a lot of  their personality and even their own  name it's this part of their programming  that has caused them to become  desensitized to the experiments they're  doing mobius then removed everything  related to him in the outside world from  the think tank so that any of the robots  in the think tank think that just big  mountain is all there is left in the  world to stop them from exploring  outside and experimenting on the mojave  dead money starts and we're kidnapped at  a brotherhood of steel bunker we're then  defeated with an explosive collar and  are told to open the sierra madre casino  or else we die the person in charge is  father elijah a former elder of the  brotherhood of steel dead money also  shows lots of key plot points like the  cloud mist that consumes the villa and  other technologies like the vending  machines holograms and the hazmat suits  the dlc also forces us to make friends  with three people being dean christine  and dog all because the explosive  collars are linked so if they die we die  and vice versa all of these three dlc  delve into a theme or topics that is  ultimately thought-provoking given the  context of the individual dlc honest  hearts explores the differences in  pacifism and aggression and how  unresolved trauma can have a lasting  impact on an individual it even dips  into some talk about religion culture  and tradition as the tribes take their  culture very seriously and the new  canaanites were actually mormon old  world blues is about a person's morals  and whether the think tanks should be  held accountable for their actions or if  dr mobius was in the right to manipulate  the think tank into believing that  there's nothing outside of big mountain  and dead money is all about greed and  letting go and not just about the money  in the casino but the casino itself as  father elijah has been obsessed with the  casino for years and he isn't willing to  let go of his dream of opening it they  all have wonderful themes and while i  prefer some of the dlc over others they  at least do an excellent job at  something whether that be the story its  characters or its setting this then  leads us to lonesome road and the reason  i gave an extreme summary of the other  three is because we're gonna be going  back to these places soon because of  this dlc lonesome road as we'll find out  is actually two stories one of the  couriers and one of ulysses when we go  near some wreckage we see the message  courier six upon coming out the other  side we see a completely destroyed town  with dust and smoke everywhere it's not  until after we exit the main building  that a voice appears  there's your signal  faint but there  just like ncr  voice without fire without strength  sick  this is ulysses the most confusing yet  most interesting person in the entire  dlc story by listening to his dialect we  notice he's a fan of caesar as he  pronounces his name kaisar ulysses also  leads us on for the entirety of the dlc  if you hate people that never explain  anything and rather speak in roundabout  ways like answering a question with a  question you will genuinely hate this  man  courier six  was career six  like you  and  not  like you  in all the ways that matter  in regards to that last statement he's  not actually wrong on top of learning  about the contract of the mojave express  in prim we also learned that some other  courier was originally going to be the  sixth one for the job but they ended up  backing out of it that was ulysses the  entire dlc revolves around us running  through the divide until we finally meet  ulysses at the end he wants us to take  our lonesome road as he calls it one  that we've taken before and he keeps  bringing that part up about being here  before and that's the main plot of this  dlc ulysses is not a fan of caesar but  he was a frumentari the same rank as  volpes he was originally a part of a  tribe and like many before him were  conquered by caesar to become the legion  as he wandered the waste as a member of  the legion he came across this community  of people elise thought of this place as  a second chance and a way of living  outside the legion but it was annexed by  the ncr so the legion sent a small group  to overtake the city and enslave  everyone ulysses wanted to save the  people of this small community but while  devising a plan the courier was sent by  the ncr to deliver a package unbeknownst  to the courier the package contained  launch codes for the icbm missiles in  the town what happened afterwards is  what we see in the game ulysses blames  us for killing his second chance at life  setting ablaze a community he finally  felt connected to all because we  delivered the device that triggered the  bombs that is ulysses story or at least  the beginning of his story after this  event around 2277 four years before new  vegas he joined up with caesar again who  ordered him to rally a tribe the white  legs this is what i meant in the  beginning about how everything is  connected whether the connection is big  or small ulysses did the same thing we  did to him we accidentally blew up his  second chance at life and he  accidentally got us caught in every  predicament in the dlc's ulysses story  continues in the same way as i ordered  the dlcs in this video which is why i  played in this sequence he rallied the  white legs tribe and attacked the new  canaanites this drove them into zion  canyon and why the white legs are in the  canyon when we arrive with the caravan  ulysses also influenced the creation of  the other dlcs after he drove out the  new canaanites ulysses continued his  journey and eventually found big  mountain when he arrived besides talking  to the think tank he also met two key  people we've already discussed christine  and elijah christine is a knight of the  brotherhood of steel's subgroup the  circle of steel we can then read up on  elijah during the brotherhood questline  back in the mojave and discovered that  he became obsessed with finding  technology that could defeat the ncr so  much so that he sat at helios 1 even  though any attack would mean their  defeat and we know the aftermath of that  since the ncr hold helios 1. elijah  escaped during this battle and was never  seen again pristine was the soldier  tasked with eliminating him elijah  stumbled upon big mountain like ulysses  did and christine followed him before  the two could confront each other she  was captured at the yangzi camp in big  mountain and was experimented on the  scars on her body are what the result  was ulysses ended up saving her by  blowing up half the facility and  eventually after a few days ran into  father elijah who told him about the  sierra madre with the intention being  that elijah would soon die after  entering the villa ulysses clearly  underestimated him going back to the  think tank when ulysses spoke to them he  asked about their history and even with  the recursion loop in their processing  they remembered all their old lives of  america and places outside big mountain  this is how both dlcs started because of  ulysses reminding the think tank of the  old world outside of big mountain that's  what caused that device we touched that  they send out to capture us and thanks  to ulysses elijah found the sierra madre  and while he lived the expedition to the  casino he couldn't open it so he needed  test subjects to open it for him so he  captured people one of them being us do  you see what i mean the courier's  actions of delivering the package  accidentally caused problems for ulysses  and ulysses actions accidentally caused  problems for the courier in light of all  the knowledge he attained from big  mountain he returned to the divide and  attempted to do what the courier did he  wants to reshape the wasteland the way  the courier reshaped the divide as he  realized how powerful a person can be  never in my life before new vegas did i  play a game that connected its dlc this  well it was absolutely genius until you  think a little harder then it gets a  little confusing ulysses gets a lot of  hate from the community mostly because  of his speech patterns but some have  claimed that it's because he was  originally a cut follower for the base  game and they didn't put enough effort  into his character because of this while  the former is true about him being cut  from the game i haven't found any  evidence to support the latter doesn't  mean it's untrue just means i couldn't  find anything but do let me know if you  do find a source the biggest reason that  some may hate him is that he's just  simply a hypocrite he's mad at us  because we nuked the divide except we  didn't we delivered the codes that  activated the nuke we weren't the ones  who pushed the button or devised the  plan we are what couriers are supposed  to be middlemen but we can say the same  for ulysses he rallied the white legs he  talked to the think tank he pointed  elijah to the sierra madre and if you  want to go one step further because he  denied the contract for the platinum  chip we almost died at the hands of  benny but here's the difference between  us and him we don't blame it on him we  blame the respective parties not ulysses  he was just simply a middleman and has  no idea his actions would have this many  consequences just like the courier's  actions also slight tangent isn't it  like an unwritten rule of like mailmen  and couriers to like not look at  people's packages ulysses was a courier  so he should know this but he still  continues to blame us ulysses is a man  who is confused unsure what to do now  that his chance that a new life is gone  instead of thinking rationally he  devises a plan not one that kills the  courier but rather mimics him we're the  courier that's been the point of this  game we're the protagonist and while the  courier explains that he settled in new  reno in california before our time with  him has been in the mojave the mojave to  us was like the divide to ulysses so  he's going to do to our home what we did  to his blow it up that's why he never  attacks us first he wants us to live  with the disaster he causes like how he  had to live with the disaster we caused  ulysses is turning into us we're pretty  much one and the same at this point  except ulysses isn't thinking properly  or rationally at all he can be seen as  the definition of insanity doing the  same thing over and over again expecting  things to change but i don't even think  ulysses wants change more revenge  revenge against the ncr and the legion  for representing new world ideals as he  despises this way of thinking and  revenge against us for taking his second  home from him fault new vegas dlc was  wonderfully crafted it seems like three  dlcs with really cool themes and  settings that added a new story and  adventure for the player to experience  giving them another reason to play new  vegas again but from the moment we step  into the sierra madre zion canyon or  even big mountain we're expecting a very  intriguing linear story that would maybe  be finished in a few hours but that  turned into one gigantic story that's  been being built in the background the  entire game a story that takes the  characters events and themes of each and  connects all of them together in a  cohesive timeline one that i haven't  seen done this well in gaming ever and  at the center of it all was the lonesome  road  fall new vegas is now what will most  likely be for the foreseeable future my  favorite game in the franchise  originally in the intro i said this  exact same line but with no reasons why  24 pages later and i hope i did a good  enough job conveying that point it may  not be your reasons but they're most  definitely mine but the moment i stepped  outside i knew new vegas was going to be  different but i never expected that to  be a good thing obsidian did an  incredible job making this game some  have even claimed it's nothing short of  a masterpiece and to an extent i'm  inclined to agree it should serve as a  blueprint for not only how fallout games  can be made but how rpgs can be made  it's a wonderful game that's a part of a  wonderful franchise from 2012 when i got  my first achievement to 2021 as i'm  writing the last few pages of this  script i've never forgotten the fun i've  had with this game and i don't think i  ever will  if you've gotten this far in the video  thank you this video took a lot longer  than expected but i hope it was worth  the wait we're not done with fallout  trust me we got tons more to talk about  so stay tuned for that if you're new  here and want to see more essay videos  like this i encourage you to check out  some of my other videos like the ones on  screen or if you want a fallout video i  have both a fallout 3 and 76 video  available for your viewing pleasure as  usual like and subscribe if you enjoyed  today's video and if you're a returning  viewer i thank you for coming back  take care everyone  goodbye  [Music]  bye
 

